{"title":"2020 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(MAA_Original_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (MAA Original Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Same_As_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Same As Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Modular_Arithmetic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Modular Arithmetic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(by_Shiva_Kumar_Kannan_-_Least_insightful_&amp;_very_straightforward_+_Manipulation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (by Shiva Kumar Kannan - Least insightful &amp; very straightforward + Manipulation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Interactive_Teaching_Approach)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Mathematical_Dexterity_(2_min)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Mathematical Dexterity (2 min)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_The_Beauty_Of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by The Beauty Of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_Using_Sophie_Germain&#39;s_Identity\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 Using Sophie Germain's Identity</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f98e39b970fbb4fcc2cb31a24d354b288822c25d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{202} +202$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a6e139d36ebcdc2d34782269826a2a992d5b10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{101}+2^{51}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc86cec5dce4ad543c35d5de7e0aff0c9c211bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 100 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 101 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 200 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 201 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 202$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"443\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28MAA_Original_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(MAA_Original_Solution)\">Solution 1 (MAA Original Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (MAA Original Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Completing the square, then difference of squares:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/86842fbd503cdcf28b8918431342f7fc4d11395c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2^{202} + 202 &amp;= (2^{101})^2 + 2\\cdot 2^{101} + 1 - 2\\cdot 2^{101} + 201\\\\ &amp;= (2^{101} + 1)^2 - 2^{102} + 201\\\\ &amp;= (2^{101} - 2^{51} + 1)(2^{101} + 2^{51} + 1) + 201. \\end{align*}\" width=\"397\" height=\"75\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThus, we see that the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/78841a1baa47be5285cdfb965296690a3ac7ba91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 201}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"75\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>(Source: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h2001950p14000817\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h2001950p14000817</a>)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c03c96b69609359d1b5087202ae9c2957f934288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2^{50}$\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />. We are now looking for the remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15e05d6191b3eabb319eae8aacaef92989781404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4x^4+202}{2x^2+2x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"102\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>We could proceed with polynomial division, but the numerator looks awfully similar to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sophie_Germain_Identity\" title=\"Sophie Germain Identity\">Sophie Germain Identity</a>,  which states that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b100b5bcacb4bcafb2d261cb92d9f8d145d89ebc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^4+4b^4=(a^2+2b^2+2ab)(a^2+2b^2-2ab)\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Let's use the identity, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb06a95428e057b1ddcda318a7768aaa73641527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=x$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, so we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d81826c91cc16610cc5b8b43a5d25dba7ac0ffe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+4x^4=(1+2x^2+2x)(1+2x^2-2x)\\]\" width=\"307\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Rearranging, we can see that this is exactly what we need:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e010372051a195c274880c199e616600c4a8ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4x^4+1}{2x^2+2x+1}=2x^2-2x+1\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be06c275b6cbeb278bb73d756532e63391bdc2af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4x^4+202}{2x^2+2x+1} = \\frac{4x^4+1}{2x^2+2x+1} +\\frac{201}{2x^2+2x+1}\\]\" width=\"354\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Since the first half divides cleanly as shown earlier, the remainder must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b03f76a2b411a6c226cf92bf79e3be20a9abd3f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }201}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"75\" height=\"28\" /> \n</p><p>~quacker88\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Same_As_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Same_As_Solution_2)\">Solution 3 (Same As Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Same As Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88a1885be9bb0c823d7ecda5c043bdc523576b53.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 2^{50}\\]\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/a/09a8c729c1e3e4141911e8962a04dc3958d5a53e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{202} + 202 = 4x^{4} + 202\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"16\" />.\nNext we write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86b6798408624ed12120a5d4e3706b6a8645f20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{101} + 2^{51} + 1 = 2x^{2} + 2x + 1\\]\" width=\"229\" height=\"16\" />.\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/7/e279d2a301df157521a9b28e83f44c7cf6ed7804.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^{4} + 1 = (2x^{2} + 2x + 1)(2x^{2} - 2x + 1)\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"19\" /> by the Sophie Germain identity so to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d4bc4d42c3498ca8e325d5704675d2320c74b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^{4} + 202,\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/2526e259f532b93b53631c6d782d98118204377f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^{4} + 202 = 4x^{4} + 201 + 1\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"16\" /> which shows that the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/78841a1baa47be5285cdfb965296690a3ac7ba91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 201}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"75\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8bf69c665d468d810bdfc444aae3359986704d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2^{50.5}$\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ff631cfd81d2eaea1824e328320cee9aa6f77a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{202}+202=x^{4}+202$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4fa089ecf7e414dc57864bcb2b2f9f78a54b68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{101}+2^{51}+1=x^{2}+2^{0.5}x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" />. Then, we simply do polynomial division, and find that the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/78841a1baa47be5285cdfb965296690a3ac7ba91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 201}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"75\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>The long division is essentially the same if you work with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, or do repeated multiplication and subtraction using the original expression.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Modular_Arithmetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Modular_Arithmetic)\">Solution 5 (Modular Arithmetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Modular Arithmetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffabe8c897f0112538dc7a224f7c271dca5d43ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2^{101}+2^{51}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />. Then, mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/1546fffff07a6170492c441fcb68603f668542ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{202}+202 \\equiv (-2^{51}-1)^2 + 202$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"245\" height=\"21\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c12bc080951eed7df50759c3d3627d2c20da703a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv 2^{102}+2^{52}+203$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f64b9833dab66cff37190e1ee5c39c86339b8420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 2(n-1)+203 \\equiv 201 \\pmod{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"262\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/78841a1baa47be5285cdfb965296690a3ac7ba91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 201}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"75\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ Leo.Euler\n</p><p>~ (edited by asops)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28by_Shiva_Kumar_Kannan_-_Least_insightful_.26_very_straightforward_.2B_Manipulation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(by_Shiva_Kumar_Kannan_-_Least_insightful_&amp;_very_straightforward_+_Manipulation)\">Solution 6 (by Shiva Kumar Kannan - Least insightful &amp; very straightforward + Manipulation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (by Shiva Kumar Kannan - Least insightful &amp; very straightforward + Manipulation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can repeatedly manipulate the numerator to make parts of it divisible by the denominator:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b9372c7cabce7dc0487a8080da47d51a451b23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2^{202}+202}{2^{101}+2^{51}+1}\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/6365a476e726a645d4ed131bcaa64582cd59979a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{2^{202} + 2^{152} + 2^{101}}{2^{101}+2^{51}+1} - \\frac{2^{152} + 2^{101} - 202}{2^{101}+2^{51}+1}\\]\" width=\"312\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cbc0c840675da537db829e98e84736c2cb4bd36.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2^{101} - \\frac{2^{152} + 2^{101} - 202}{2^{101}+2^{51}+1}\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/05060c4ae952d9b1d0b86612b6bb745838238e0c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=2^{101} - \\frac{2^{152}+2^{101}+2^{101}+2^{51} - 2^{101} - 2^{51} - 202}{2^{101}+2^{51}+1}\\]\" width=\"398\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b450c32ad35aae442f3be996727b044cb28c0776.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=2^{101} - 2^{51} + \\frac{2^{101}+2^{51}+202}{2^{101}+2^{51}+1}\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1ea6aed1e224966f70c16f2579433cfcc77e117.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2^{101} - 2^{51} + \\frac{2^{101}+2^{51}+1+201}{2^{101}+2^{51}+1}\\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/39690bf872a1427f4ee6e344d274db50c098d744.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2^{101} - 2^{51} + 1 + \\frac{201}{2^{101} + 2^{51} + 1}.\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/70912f51d47102628dae37f161a9bf46b191bd41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$201 &lt; 2^{201} + 2^{51} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />, hence, we cannot manipulate the numerator further to make the denominator divide into one of its parts. This concludes, that the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/78841a1baa47be5285cdfb965296690a3ac7ba91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 201}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"75\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Interactive_Teaching_Approach.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Interactive_Teaching_Approach)\">Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Oc4aNpPlnkA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Oc4aNpPlnkA</a>\n</p><p>~MathkidsbyMax\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Mathematical_Dexterity_.282_min.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Mathematical_Dexterity_(2_min)\">Video Solution 1 by Mathematical Dexterity (2 min)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Mathematical Dexterity (2 min)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lLWURnmpPQA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lLWURnmpPQA</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_The_Beauty_Of_Math\">Video Solution 2 by The Beauty Of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by The Beauty Of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gPqd-yKQdFg\">https://youtu.be/gPqd-yKQdFg</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qs6UnryIAI8&amp;list=PLLCzevlMcsWNcTZEaxHe8VaccrhubDOlQ&amp;index=9&amp;t=0s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qs6UnryIAI8&amp;list=PLLCzevlMcsWNcTZEaxHe8VaccrhubDOlQ&amp;index=9&amp;t=0s</a> ~ MathEx\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Video_Solution_4_Using_Sophie_Germain.27s_Identity\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4_Using_Sophie_Germain's_Id